# Coda Formula Customizer - Vue d'ensemble

Extension Chrome (Manifest V3, v2.0.0) qui personnalise l'editeur de formules Coda.

## Stack technique

- **Popup** : React 19 + JSX + CSS variables
- **Content script** : JavaScript ES6+ vanilla (MutationObserver, DOM manipulation)
- **Build** : Vite 5 + @crxjs/vite-plugin + @vitejs/plugin-react
- **Stockage** : chrome.storage.local
- **Communication** : chrome.runtime.onMessage / chrome.tabs.sendMessage

## Structure

```
src/shared/config.js              → DEFAULT_CONFIG, validateConfig, mergeConfig (source unique)
src/shared/storage.js             → StorageManager (ACID, partage popup + content)
src/content/index.js              → Point d'entree content script
src/content/style-manager.js      → StyleManager (CSS, themes, indent guides)
src/content/dom-selector.js       → DOMSelector (queries DOM Coda)
src/content/modal-size-manager.js → ModalSizeManager (taille/position modale)
src/content/layout-manager.js     → LayoutManager (disposition documentation)
src/content/dialog-processor.js   → DialogProcessor (Facade)
src/content/modal-customizer.js   → ModalCustomizer (Observer, MutationObserver)
src/popup/App.jsx                 → Composant racine React
src/popup/hooks/useChromeStorage.js → Hook sync chrome.storage <-> React state
src/popup/components/*.jsx        → Composants UI (Header, Accordion, panels, etc.)
```

## Build

```bash
npm run dev      # Dev server avec HMR
npm run build    # Production → dist/
```

Le plugin @crxjs/vite-plugin lit manifest.json et gere automatiquement les entry points (popup React + content script IIFE).
